    <solution><me>\mathbf{r}'(t)=\langle 5,-6,5\rangle</me>
and so
<me>||\mathbf{r}'(t)||=\sqrt{5^2+(-6)^2+5^2}=\sqrt{86}.</me>
The unit tangent vector is therefore:
<me>\mathbf{T}(t)
=\frac{\mathbf{r}'(t)}{||\mathbf{r}'(t)||}
= \frac{1}{\sqrt{86}}\langle 5,-6,5\rangle
=\left\langle \frac{5}{\sqrt{86}}, \frac{-6}{\sqrt{86}}, \frac{5}{\sqrt{86}} \right\rangle.</me>
We see that the unit tangent is constant, since the curve is a straight line.


</solution>
